<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">02072026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Russia launched ballistic missiles, cruise missiles and drones across five districts of the Kyiv region overnight, killing two people and wounding eleven.</s> <s>It's the first strike on Ukraine's capital in two weeks, and it came just hours after Zelenskyy warned Moscow was preparing a major assault.</s> <s>Poland scrambled fighter jets to guard its own airspace as rescuers dug through a collapsed building — the war's tempo still set by Moscow's air campaign, not the negotiating table.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Myanmar's civil war has now killed more than one hundred thousand people since the two thousand twenty-one coup, one monitor says.</s> <s>The junta is fighting over one thousand two hundred armed groups, making it the world's most fragmented conflict and Asia's deadliest.</s> <s>General Min Aung Hlaing's call for peace talks was rejected by rebels as image-laundering, with no ceasefire in sight.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Sudan's North Darfur, five hundred forty-four families fled their homes in just three days, now living in the open without shelter or water.</s> <s>The Rapid Support Forces seized the towns of Orshi and Ambro while the army-aligned Joint Force took Abu Qamra, scattering civilians across the desert.</s> <s>Karnoi's emergency room has appealed for humanitarian corridors as hundreds more families remain trapped.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Iran and the United States remain deadlocked over six billion dollars in Iranian funds frozen in Qatar.</s> <s>Tehran wants the money released in two tranches, while Washington has proposed restricting it to American agricultural purchases — an offer it rejects.</s> <s>Technical teams are meeting again through Qatari and Pakistani mediation, but the frozen assets stay the sticking point.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In South Africa's Western Cape, three hundred people are sheltering in a community hall after landlords evicted them in an anti-immigrant campaign.</s> <s>Activists went door to door threatening residents who housed foreigners, most of them Malawians now waiting for buses home.</s> <s>Officials haven't said when repatriation will happen, leaving families stranded between two countries.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>China's foreign direct investment has fallen thirty-nine percent, according to UN figures.</s> <s>Two State Council decrees issued since two thousand twenty-two now impose criminal liability on executives who cut ties with Chinese suppliers, unnerving foreign firms.</s> <s>Beijing hasn't said whether it will ease the rules if the investment slide continues.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>South Korea's outgoing prime minister is angling to become chairman of the ruling Democratic Party.</s> <s>The contest comes as friction grows between the presidential office and the party's rank and file.</s> <s>Who wins will shape whether Seoul's next policy direction runs through the president or through the party.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>The European Union has ended its duty-free treatment of low-value parcels, imposing a flat three-euro fee on packages worth under one hundred fifty euros.</s> <s>That exemption had let retailers like Shein and Temu ship an estimated five point eight billion parcels a year direct from China untaxed.</s> <s>The flat fee runs until twenty twenty-eight, when category-specific duties take over.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The new US Federal Reserve chair, Kevin Warsh, has vowed no changes to the central bank's independence, speaking at a forum in Portugal.</s> <s>Appointed after Trump pressured his predecessor over interest rates, Warsh insisted the bank stays committed to two percent inflation whatever the White House says.</s> <s>Traders are now betting on an October rate hike after fresh government data.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Four advocacy groups are suing the French energy giant TotalEnergies to reveal the terms of its exit from Nigeria's oil fields.</s> <s>France's Duty of Vigilance Law requires the firm to prevent harm from selling its Niger Delta assets to a local buyer.</s> <s>A French court will now decide whether Total must disclose who pays to clean up the delta's decades of oil spills.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The World Bank has approved seventy million dollars to expand broadband across Pakistan's Punjab province.</s> <s>This loan cuts permitting time for network construction from ninety days to twenty-one, aiming to connect two point one million more people by twenty thirty-one.</s> <s>It also targets tripling women's use of digital government services — a quiet test of whether connectivity narrows the gender gap.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>The world's oceans just recorded their hottest June ever, with marine heatwaves striking eighty-two percent of the sea surface.</s> <s>A new El Niño is stacking on top of rising background heat, pushing temperatures past both twenty twenty-three and twenty twenty-four records, Europe's Copernicus service says.</s> <s>Scientists expect more records to fall, worsening droughts and cyclones in the months ahead.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Researchers in Barcelona have built wireless microchips that can stimulate a single living cell using sound.</s> <s>These piezoelectric devices convert ultrasound into electrical signals, activating cells without wires or surgical implants.</s> <s>The approach opens a path toward noninvasive, targeted therapies for conditions that today demand invasive electrodes.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The French rocket firm Latitude will launch its first vehicle from Oman, making the sultanate the second Gulf state to host a European launch company.</s> <s>It follows another European firm signing with Oman's Etlaq spaceport last year.</s> <s>Neither company has said how the buildout will be funded ahead of a twenty twenty-seven debut, God willing.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Sony will stop selling PlayStation games on disc from January twenty twenty-eight, shifting entirely to digital licenses.</s> <s>That means buyers can no longer resell, lend, or even keep a game once their access is revoked.</s> <s>Loyal players already angry over subscription price hikes now face a library they license but never truly own.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Researchers in Sydney found that twenty-five major language models converge on nearly identical answers — ask any of them for a random number, and it's seven.</s> <s>The reason is a kind of groupthink: most models train on similar data for similar tasks, a finding that won a top AI award.</s> <s>One startup has built a rival model that deliberately injects randomness to break the pattern.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>